Here is a WordPress plugin that clears all Nginx Helper Cache when a plugin or theme is added, updated, or changed:
```php
<?php
/*
Plugin Name: Nginx Helper Cache Clearer
Description: Clears all Nginx Helper Cache when a plugin or theme is added, updated, or changed
Version: 1.0
Author: Your Name
Author URI: https://yourwebsite.com
*/

// Hook to clear cache when a plugin is activated, deactivated, or updated
add_action('plugins_loaded', 'nginx_helper_cache_clearer_plugins_loaded');
function nginx_helper_cache_clearer_plugins_loaded() {
    if (wp_doing_cron() || defined('WP_INSTALLING')) {
        return;
    }

    // Clear cache when a plugin is activated
    add_action('activate_plugin', 'nginx_helper_cache_clearer_clear_cache');
    // Clear cache when a plugin is deactivated
    add_action('deactivate_plugin', 'nginx_helper_cache_clearer_clear_cache');
    // Clear cache when a plugin is updated
    add_action('upgrader_process_complete', 'nginx_helper_cache_clearer_clear_cache');
}

// Hook to clear cache when a theme is switched
add_action('switch_theme', 'nginx_helper_cache_clearer_clear_cache');

// Function to clear Nginx Helper Cache
function nginx_helper_cache_clearer_clear_cache() {
    // Get the Nginx Helper Cache directory
    $cache_dir = WP_CONTENT_DIR . '/cache/nginx-helper';

    // Check if the cache directory exists
    if (file_exists($cache_dir)) {
        // Clear the cache directory
        $files = glob($cache_dir . '/*');
        foreach ($files as $file) {
            if (is_file($file)) {
                unlink($file);
            }
        }
    }

    // Send a PURGE request to Nginx to clear the cache
    $url = home_url('/');
    $headers = array(
        'Host' => $_SERVER['HTTP_HOST'],
        'Cache-Control' => 'no-cache',
        'Pragma' => 'no-cache',
        'Expires' => '-1',
    );
    $args = array(
        'method' => 'PURGE',
        'headers' => $headers,
    );
    wp_remote_request($url, $args);

    // Log the cache clear event
    error_log('Nginx Helper Cache cleared');
}

// Hook to clear cache when a theme is updated
add_action('upgrader_process_complete', 'nginx_helper_cache_clearer_clear_cache_theme');
function nginx_helper_cache_clearer_clear_cache_theme($upgrader_object) {
    if ($upgrader_object->update['use_theme'] === true) {
        nginx_helper_cache_clearer_clear_cache();
    }
}
```
This plugin uses the following hooks to clear the Nginx Helper Cache:

* `activate_plugin`: when a plugin is activated
* `deactivate_plugin`: when a plugin is deactivated
* `upgrader_process_complete`: when a plugin is updated
* `switch_theme`: when a theme is switched
* `upgrader_process_complete` (with `use_theme` check): when a theme is updated

The `nginx_helper_cache_clearer_clear_cache` function clears the Nginx Helper Cache directory and sends a PURGE request to Nginx to clear the cache.

Note: You'll need to update the `WP_CONTENT_DIR` constant to point to the correct directory where your WordPress content is stored.

Also, make sure to test this plugin in a staging environment before using it in production.

You can install this plugin by creating a new file in the `wp-content/plugins` directory, naming it `nginx-helper-cache-clearer.php`, and pasting the above code into it. Then, activate the plugin in the WordPress admin dashboard.

